---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import BookingLink from '../../components/BookingLink.astro';
import DiscoveryCall from '../../components/DiscoveryCall.astro';
---
<SiteLayout service="consulting" title="Business automation consulting | TJ Maynes" description="Automate recurring reports, connect systems, and build AI workflows your team can operate. Remote consulting with a defined scope, validation, and handoff.">
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="consulting-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Business automation consulting</p><h1 id="consulting-title">Spend less of your week moving work between tools.</h1>
      <p class="lead">I help founders, business leaders, and engineering managers turn recurring manual work into tested workflows. We’ll start with one process and agree on what a useful result looks like.</p>
      <div class="actions"><BookingLink service="consulting" placement="hero" /><span class="call-note">Free · 15 minutes · Video call</span></div><p class="small hero-note">Tell me what repeats, where it gets stuck, and what you’d like to change.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Problems we can work on</p><h2 id="work-title">Start with the work that keeps coming back.</h2></div>
      <div class="example-list">
        <article><h3>Recurring reports</h3><p>Your team copies figures into spreadsheets or writes the same update every week. We can collect the data, validate it, and prepare a draft for review.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Disconnected systems</h3><p>A request arrives in one tool and someone re-enters it in another. We can connect those steps and make failures visible to the person responsible.</p></article>
        <article><h3>AI in an existing workflow</h3><p>You have a use case for drafting, extraction, or classification. We can test it against representative examples, add review points, and decide whether it is reliable enough to use.</p></article>
      </div><p class="section-link"><a href="/#report-demo">Try a small reporting demonstration <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap split" aria-labelledby="process-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">How a project works</p><h2 id="process-title">A clear scope, then a working handoff.</h2></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Understand one workflow</h3><p>We map the current steps, systems, exceptions, and who owns the result. We agree on how to check whether the change helps.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Agree on scope and price</h3><p>You receive deliverables, acceptance checks, dependencies, and a fixed-price quote. If the unknowns are too large, I’ll quote a smaller paid assessment first.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Build and review together</h3><p>I build in small steps, demonstrate progress, and test failures as well as the expected path. We decide where human approval belongs.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Hand it over</h3><p>You get the workflow, documentation, and a walkthrough. We agree on ownership, access, and any ongoing support before launch.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap split" aria-labelledby="pricing-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Pricing and ownership</p><h2 id="pricing-title">Know what you’re buying before work starts.</h2></div>
      <div class="prose"><p>Implementation is quoted by scope. The fee covers the agreed build, validation, documentation, and handoff. Changes to that scope need a separate agreement.</p><p>Software subscriptions, hosting, and AI/API usage are separate unless the quote explicitly includes them. I’ll make those costs visible before you commit.</p><p>Your business should control its accounts and workflows. Ongoing monitoring, maintenance, and response commitments are agreed separately; they are not assumed to be included forever.</p><p>For an engineering team, I can pair with your developers and include them in the evaluation and handoff. If you want to build your own skills one-to-one, see <a href="/services/coaching/">AI coaching</a>.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap split" aria-labelledby="consulting-faq-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p><h2 id="consulting-faq-title">Before we scope it</h2></div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>Do we have to use AI?</summary><p>No. Many useful automations are integrations and straightforward rules. We’ll use AI where it serves the task and test the parts that can vary.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can you work with our existing tools and team?</summary><p>That is the starting point. We’ll check the available integrations and access together, then decide whether custom code or another tool is needed.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How long will a project take?</summary><p>I’ll give you a delivery estimate after we understand the scope, access, and dependencies. The discovery call helps us decide what needs investigating before I can quote it.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <DiscoveryCall service="consulting" title="Which workflow would you change first?" />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
